---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { atlas as idx } from "../lib/atlas.js";
import provs from "../../public/providers.json";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import full from "../data/places-full.json";
import "../styles/kit.css";
/* EVERY NUMBER ON THIS PAGE IS COUNTED, as on /about/. The one typed fact is the start month. The donation link lives in
   src/data/site.json (support.url): it is a hosted Stripe Payment Link, so the payment happens on Stripe's page and this page
   never sees a card. check-data.py refuses the sandbox link (/test_), so the page cannot ship with it. */
const dots = idx.places.length;
const countries = new Set(full.places.map((p) => p.country).filter(Boolean)).size;
const sources = provs.providers.length;
const url = site.support?.url || "";
---
<Base
  title="Support Record Atlas"
  eyebrow="Free to use, and free to keep"
  dek="What this project is, what it takes to keep it going, and what a gift does. Nothing on the atlas is locked, whether or not you give.">

  <div class="k-hi">
    <p>Record Atlas is free. It has no paywall, no account and no subscription, and that will not change.</p>
    <p>It is kept going by one person. If it has saved you an evening, a gift of any size helps keep it going.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="sp-cta"><a class="sp-btn" href={url} rel="noopener">Give a gift</a>
  <span>You choose the amount. Paid on Stripe's own page; this site never sees your card.</span></p>

  <h2 class="k-h">How much work it is</h2>
  <div class="k-stats" aria-label="The atlas in numbers">
    <span><b>{dots.toLocaleString()}</b> places</span>
    <span><b>{countries}</b> countries</span>
    <span><b>{sources.toLocaleString()}</b> sources</span>
    <span class="k-tag">started September 2026</span>
  </div>
  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>Each source is read, placed on the map, checked against the place's name in the year of the record, and marked with what it costs to look.
    Every figure on the atlas is counted from its data, never typed, and a build that finds a gap stops rather than publishing it.</p>
    <p>Most of it is slow, careful reading: which archive holds a register, whether the images are free, what a place was called in 1890.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="k-h">About me</h2>
  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>I am David Defranceski. I research family history, mostly my own: the Defranceschi name, which runs from Istria and Dalmatia through Friuli to the Americas, and a few other families I have been asked to help with. I do it on my own, with no institution behind me.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="k-h">Why I built it</h2>
  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>Every family I worked on ran into the same wall: which archive holds the register for a village, whether its images are free to read, and what the place was called in the year of the record. I would spend an evening in a book and find that it had already been read, or that it was not the book its catalogue title claimed. I built the atlas so that what one search learns is kept for the next, whoever makes it.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="k-h">Why it is free</h2>
  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>Research that only people who can pay can find is research that gets repeated. A paywall would have broken the one thing the atlas is for: a stranger can find, on any evening, the register a family needs, and add what they learned back. I would rather it was used than earned from.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="k-h">What it costs to run</h2>
  <ul class="k-tiles sp-tiles">
    <li><b>Hosting</b><span>US$5 a month for Cloudflare's paid plan, which serves every page. It is billed per request once the site passes 10 million a month, so it grows as more people use it.</span></li>
    <li><b>Records</b><span>Some sources sit behind a subscription. When a question cannot be answered from free records I take one out for a month, rather than keep it running.</span></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="k-h">What a gift does</h2>
  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>A gift goes first to the hosting bill, which grows if the atlas gets busy, and then to the occasional month of a records subscription when a question needs one.</p>
    <p>A gift does not buy a feature, early access or a place in the queue. It keeps the atlas running and lets the work go on.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="sp-cta"><a class="sp-btn" href={url} rel="noopener">Give a gift</a>
  <span>You choose the amount. Stripe handles the payment.</span></p>

  <div class="k-foot">
    <p>Good to know</p>
    <p>A gift is a personal gift to the person who runs this atlas, not a tax-deductible donation to a charity.
    <a href={u("/privacy/")}>Privacy</a> · <a href={u("/about/")}>About the atlas</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .sp-cta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 4px 0 26px; }
  .sp-cta span { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .sp-btn { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent); color: #fff; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 16px; }
  .sp-btn:hover, .sp-btn:focus-visible { background: var(--accent-2); }
  .sp-tiles { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); max-width: 980px; }
  .sp-tiles li > span { display: block; }
  .sp-tiles li b { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }
  .k-stats > span { white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
